WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.040
We're here with the contributing editor

2
00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.240
of one of my favorite magazines on planet earth,

3
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.300
House Beautiful, and founder of Kingston Design Connection,

4
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.463
Interior Designer, Maryline Damour.

5
00:00:10.347 --> 00:00:12.678
(audience cheering and applauding)

6
00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:16.320
All right, you've just helped a viewer on their dining room.

7
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.200
Yes, I did.

8
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.299
To great success, in my opinion.

9
00:00:19.299 --> 00:00:20.420
Oh, thank you.

10
00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.470
And we have an audience member

11
00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:25.730
who has a little design dilemma, in a special Drew &amp; A.

12
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.110
Where is Tamara Lynch?

13
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.623
Right here.
Hello!

14
00:00:31.148 --> 00:00:32.710
(audience applauding)
Hi Drew.

15
00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:34.820
My flower sees your flower.

16
00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.010
I am a passionate flower lover,

17
00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:40.250
so I am so happy to be here with you.

18
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.830
What is your design question, so everybody knows?

19
00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:47.830
So, I have this sofa. I've had her for over 12 years.

20
00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.933
And if you sit in my couch, you sink into it.

21
00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.550
What's significant about this couch,

22
00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:55.640
you know, people will be like,

23
00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.740
oh, just throw it away, and get a new one.

24
00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.330
It's not that easy, you know?

25
00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:03.930
I lost my job to the pandemic,

26
00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:08.260
I worked as a restaurant worker, and then was basically told

27
00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:12.030
to sit down on March 16th, 2020.

28
00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.640
And when my job came back,

29
00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.130 line:15%
we only took 25% of the workforce.

30
00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:18.880 line:15%
So it was a different life for me.

31
00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.990 line:15%
I spent a lotta time depressed on this couch.

32
00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:25.290
But I've always been a resilient person,

33
00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:29.450
and I just feel like putting one foot in front of the other

34
00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:33.780
is just, even when you can't see where you're going,

35
00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:35.000
you just do it.

36
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.920
And while I was on that couch,
(audience applauding)

37
00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:42.850
I did something watching your show,

38
00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:46.380
which was just go online and say,

39
00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.833
put my name like just a random place.

40
00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:55.550
And to be given a gift, like just for your phone to ring,

41
00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:59.620
and say, "Hi, I have a random act of kindness for you,"

42
00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:04.620
has been, just profound.

43
00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.459
Profound. It has been profound.

44
00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:08.799
(audience applauding)

45
00:02:08.799 --> 00:02:10.110
That's all I can say.

46
00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.390
I love your attitude of putting one foot

47
00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:13.310
in front of the other.

48
00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:15.880
Your sentimentality towards this couch

49
00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:17.660
is completely understandable.

50
00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:20.450
But telling your story, for me, is the key,

51
00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:22.261
so thank you so much for sharing it-

52
00:02:22.261 --> 00:02:26.420
Thank you, thank you so much. Thank you, really.

53
00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:29.510
And it's not trivial to pivot to the couch.

54
00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:33.510
I'm lucky that we are here with one of my design heroes.

55
00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.610
I would love to know,

56
00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:37.380
especially with that beautiful back story,

57
00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.630
now what, Maryline?

58
00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:41.710
Yeah, no. So I really, really wanted to honor your sofa.

59
00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:43.730 line:15%
I love that it's a part of your family.

60
00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.850 line:15%
And so one of the first things I did was to cover it

61
00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:49.000 line:15%
in one of the most hard wearing fabrics out there,

62
00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.210
which is linen.

63
00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:53.770 line:15%
So linen will last you for many, many years to come,

64
00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:57.460 line:15%
and then there's some colorful pillows on top.

65
00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:00.500
And the other thing is, you didn't previously have a carpet,

66
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.410
and I know in smaller spaces

67
00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.240
people tend to think of adding less,

68
00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:07.780 line:15%
but really defining a space, it's kinda counterintuitive,

69
00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:09.830 line:15%
but it actually helps to give you the look and feel

70
00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:10.760 line:15%
of a bigger space.

71
00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.890 line:15%
And it defines it as a real living room.

72
00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:15.890 line:15%
So bringing that carpet in is really important.

73
00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:20.390 line:15%
The other thing that you didn't have was a coffee table,

74
00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:22.350
so the coffee table's important,

75
00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.590
because it just makes the space more functional.

76
00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:26.930
And you can actually find these sometimes with shelves,

77
00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:28.800
so it gives you a little bit more storage.

78
00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.170
So I brought that in as well.

79
00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:35.270
And overall, the idea is to really honor your living room,

80
00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:38.550
to make it a place that you can continue to add to

81
00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:39.520
over the years.

82
00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:42.400
So you can imagine a brightly covered throw,

83
00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.490 line:15%
more flowers, some artwork.

84
00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.370 line:15%
But you know, the sofa will really become kinda the anchor

85
00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:48.828 line:15%
of your space.

86
00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:50.842 line:15%
Thank you, that's beautiful.
(audience applauding)

87
00:03:50.842 --> 00:03:52.259
That's beautiful.

88
00:03:54.071 --> 00:03:55.053
That's gorgeous.

89
00:03:55.053 --> 00:03:57.832
What do you think, Tamara?

90
00:03:57.832 --> 00:03:59.300
That's gorgeous.
(Tamara chuckles)

91
00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.050
Do you like it?
That's really beautiful.

92
00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:04.663
I just love the coolness of it. That is beautiful.

93
00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:06.770
Thank you.
I love it.

94
00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:09.500
And you're absolutely right, the more you add

95
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:12.190
into a small space, the bigger it seems.

96
00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:14.370
It's counterintuitive indeed.
Yeah, it's weird.

97
00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:15.810
But it's true. Pack it.

98
00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:18.080
I love it. I hope you do too.
(audience applauding)

99
00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:21.093
Yeah, I do. I think it's so sophisticated.

100
00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:23.210
All right. Well, thank God.

101
00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:25.200
Because it's all going home with you.

102
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.030
Every single thing in this room,

103
00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:29.590
we are putting in your living room.

104
00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:32.194
The coffee table, the couch, the pillows,

105
00:04:32.194 --> 00:04:33.800
the throws, everything.

106
00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:37.710
And we have $2,000 for you to do whatever you want with,

107
00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.475
and then I'm gonna match it, so that's four.

108
00:04:39.475 --> 00:04:40.335
Oh my gosh.
(audience applauding)

109
00:04:40.335 --> 00:04:41.806
And let's just round it up to five.

110
00:04:41.806 --> 00:04:46.460
Where it's just five for you to do with it as you see fit,

111
00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:50.893
to make your home life a little bit brighter.

112
00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:57.150
And I thank you so much. Really and truly.

113
00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:58.493
You're a blessing.
(audience applauding)

114
00:04:58.493 --> 00:05:00.243
You're just an angel.

115
00:05:00.243 --> 00:05:03.570 line:15%
And Maryline, thank you, as always, so much.

116
00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.500 line:15%
Oh, thank you.
You're just so amazing.

117
00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:06.399 line:15%
Oh, thank you.
(Maryline chuckles)

118
00:05:06.399 --> 00:05:09.334 line:15%
It looks so sophisticated.
Thank you.

119
00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:13.001 line:15%
(bright upbeat theme music)

